= An Attempt on Senator Amidala

A bomb destroys Senator Amidala's ship on its landing platform on Coruscant. She survives because she was disguised as one of her pilots; her decoy, Cordé, does not. A second attempt follows days later. Padmé was on her way to vote against the Military Creation Act.

The Chancellor offers her the protection of the Jedi: Obi-Wan Kenobi and his apprentice, Anakin Skywalker.

- @jedi: Accept the Jedi's protection.
- @naboo: Rely on Naboo's own security and go into hiding.
- @investigate: Track down whoever hired the assassin.

@jedi
subtitle: She will be safe. Anakin will be very close to her.
on-arrival: padme_jedi_guard = 1; anakin_fall += 0.3

Anakin Skywalker is given the job of escorting Senator Amidala back to Naboo. He has not seen her in ten years. He has thought about her every day.

@naboo
subtitle: Safer from scandal; Anakin feels shut out.
on-arrival: anakin_fall += 0.5; padme_hidden = 1

Padmé retreats to the Lake Country under Naboo's own guards. Anakin, refused the assignment, sulks at the Temple and confides in the Chancellor.

@investigate
subtitle: −1 political capital. Follows the trail.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 1; padme_jedi_guard = 1; evidence += 0.8; kamino_hunt += 1

The assassin, a changeling named Zam Wesell, is killed by her employer before she can talk: a bounty hunter in Mandalorian armour, using a toxic dart that only one world in the galaxy manufactures. The trail leads somewhere beyond the Rishi Maze.
